---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Project Development: Land Access & Stakeholder Facilitation"
  description="Full project proposals from land access through bringing local and international stakeholders together."
>
  <section class="section service-page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow"><a href="/what-we-do">&larr; What We Do</a></p>
      <h1 class="reveal">04 &middot; Project Development: Land Access &amp; Stakeholder Facilitation</h1>
      <p class="lede reveal">
        A mining project rarely fails on geology alone. It fails on land
        access nobody secured properly, or stakeholders who were never
        brought into the same conversation. We build the project proposal
        that accounts for both from the start.
      </p>

      <div class="body-grid">
        <div class="reveal">
          <h2>What this covers</h2>
          <p>
            Land access work: identifying who actually holds rights or
            claims to a piece of land, whether formal titleholders,
            customary authorities, or artisanal miners already working it,
            and building an access agreement that holds up because
            everyone with a real stake in it was consulted.
          </p>
          <p>
            Full project proposals that bring together the pieces an
            investor, government partner or community expects to see in
            one place: land status, community and traditional authority
            engagement, environmental and social baseline, and a realistic
            development sequence.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal">
          <h2>How we work</h2>
          <p>
            Stakeholder facilitation sits at the centre of this work:
            bringing local communities, traditional authorities, government
            bodies and international investors or partners into a single
            shared process, where agreements are tested against every
            party's expectations at the same table.
          </p>
          <p>
            Because we operate our own ASM site and work across the sector
            in Sub-Saharan Africa, we bring a working knowledge of how
            local land and authority structures actually function on the
            ground, alongside how a land registry describes them on paper.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="pill-btn" href="/contact">Talk to us about your project</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .service-page .eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .lede {
    max-width: 720px;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin-bottom: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }

  .body-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--gap);
    margin-bottom: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
  }

  .cta-row {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top: 2rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .body-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
